## A practical embodied-assistant architecture

```text
wake word / push-to-talk
    -> microphone (USB / Pi / ESP32 I2S / voice satellite)
    -> STT (Whisper / faster-whisper / local STT)
    -> dialogue + intents + permissions
    -> Home Assistant or MQTT actions
    -> expressive output router:
          voice -> fast speaker / Piper / cloud TTS
          Furby -> fluffkit / PyFluff (eyes, antenna, gestures, preloaded lines)
          locomotion -> Roomba OI / MiP BLE / Sphero SDK
          lights -> WLED / Tasmota / ESPHome
          face -> OpenEPaperLink / tablet display / LED matrix
```

**Principle:** Keep the intelligence and speech system off the toy at first; let it be a safe, replaceable actuator-and-sensor body. This works even if the toy's own processor is tiny or closed. Add real-time speech through the original speaker only if you later find and verify a feasible hardware-level audio interface.

